    "intro_html":  "Picadinho is what a Brazilian kitchen makes when it wants beef stew without waiting all afternoon. The beef gets diced small instead of cubed large, which means more browned surface, faster cooking, and a piece of meat in every single spoonful. Carrots and sweet potato round it out. Each bowl carries \u003cstrong\u003e44 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e and 566 calories for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.49\u003c/strong\u003e.",
